{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792300000000-review-6b-fix1.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-Local: 2026-10-13 00:25 +07\n# Re-review (mutation method): slice 6b after fix round 1\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6b`, branch `srvm-phase6b`, HEAD a396f996 (fix commit on top of c3d37586). Your previous findings: `collab/1792280000000-review-6b-task-transport.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md` (F1-F5). Opus's fix report: `collab/1792290000000-engineer-6b-fix1.report.md`. Verify each of F1-F5 is truly fixed by rerunning YOUR OWN reproductions (the recipes in your findings: re-emitted row-1 carrier with store `yin/def`, closure entry 999999999, row 10 retained response `{}` and phase `:bogus`, the `ghost` + unrelated module store case, custody + missing trees), and look for NEW defects the fix introduced: (a) the staged check order across the whole task tree (store, pendings, dependencies, custody) against sections 3.3 and 7.2; (b) the new `attaches?` check (discarded `module/attach-module` on the receiver): can it have side effects on the receiver, double-count work, or refuse a valid vector the real attach accepts; (c) the per-context discharge: contexts for closures/acts/return frames, tail states, nested bodies, the resolve order (own E, the one active-store, primitive, installing export, registry); try states where the old union rule accepted and the new one refuses a VALID state (false refusals) and states that still wrongly pass; (d) install validation: any valid install state refused; (e) the harness attach-count law is not vacuous. Own mutants (cp backup, diff and git diff --quiet to verify restore): drop each staged check; restore the union discharge; skip the install-phase check; run custody first; attach before closure check; make the attach-count law always pass. Say which survive. Also portability read of the new code for Node/Dart. Run `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test` and `-i :slow`, foreground. Findings file `collab/1792300000000-review-6b-fix1.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md` ending VERDICT: READY_TO_MERGE or CHANGES_REQUESTED. Edit nothing else.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
