{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '100,150p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '200,222p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '395,445p' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc; sed -n '448,465p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md; sed -n '1010,1100p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md; cat src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/scan.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"        {:reason :marker-mismatch, :segment (:yin.k/segment marker)}))\n\n\n(defn continuation-argument\n  \"The one value a captured continuation is applied to. Applying a\n   continuation is abortive: the current continuation is discarded and\n   the argument becomes the value of the capture point. Every VM refuses\n   any other arity with this same message.\"\n  [args]\n  (when-not (= 1 (count args))\n    (throw (ex-info \"Continuation expects exactly one argument\"\n                    {:reason :continuation-arity, :argc (count args)})))\n  (first args))\n\n\n(defn resolve-var\n  \"Look up a variable name: env -> store -> primitives -> module registry.\n\n   A reserved name (Rule R: `yin/def` is syntax, never a name) is refused\n   before env or store is consulted, so no binding, store entry, or\n   registry can give it a meaning. Every executing variable lookup of\n   every engine goes through here.\n\n   The registry is a value supplied by the composition, not a global.\"\n  [env store primitives registry name]\n  (when (vm/reserved-name? name)\n    (vm/refuse-reserved! :variable name))\n  (if-let [pair (find env name)]\n    (val pair)\n    (if-let [pair (find store name)]\n      (val pair)\n      (if-let [pair (find primitives name)]\n        (vm/primitive-function (val pair))\n        (if-let [resolved (when (namespace name)\n                            (module/resolve-module\n                              registry\n                              (symbol (str (namespace name)\n                                           \".\"\n                                           (clojure.core/name name)))))]\n          resolved\n          (fail (str \"Unable to resolve symbol: \" name \" in this context\")\n                {:symbol name}))))))\n\n\n(defn check-store-key!\n  \"Refuse a program store access whose key is a reserved name (Rule R):\n   the definition operator is never a store key.\"\n  [key]\n  (when (vm/reserved-name? key)\n    (vm/refuse-reserved! :store-key key)))\n\n   environment.\"\n  [state]\n  (or (:store-of state) (env-store-of (:env state))))\n\n\n(defn active-store\n  \"The store free reads and `:store-get` resolve against: while a module\n   closure runs (`store-of` non-nil), its module store, with no ambient\n   fallback -- a key the module store lacks is absent; otherwise the\n   task's own store.\"\n  [state store-of]\n  (if (some? store-of)\n    (get (:module-stores state) store-of {})\n    (:store state)))\n\n\n(defn put-active\n  \"Write `key` in the active store of `state`: the module store\n   `store-of` names, or the task's own store at top level. Both go\n   through `store-put`, so a reserved key is refused either way.\"\n  [state store-of key val]\n  (if (some? store-of)\n    (update-in state [:module-stores store-of]\n(defprotocol IModuleKernel\n  \"What a kernel supplies the install child and the `linked` transition\n   (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3). Every method is a pure function of a\n   VM value; the engine owns the phases, the kernel owns its coordinates.\"\n\n  (link-format\n    [vm]\n    \"`{:format kw :contract s}`: the format this kernel links, and the\n     execution contract it runs.\")\n\n  (spawn-module\n    [vm image opts]\n    \"A fresh VM of this backend with the verified `image` loaded by the\n     ordinary loader, holding nothing of `vm`'s state but its composition\n     values (primitives, stream constructor, link pair). `opts` carries\n     `:modules` (the child's module view), `:origin`, and `:ancestry`.\")\n\n  (image-identity\n    [vm image]\n    \"The identity this kernel's code space names `image` by: H, R, the\n     vector's address, or the tree's root row id.\")\n\n  (image-holds?\n    [vm image segment]\n    \"True when a closure marker's `:yin.k/segment` falls in `image`.\")\n\n  (attach-module\n    [vm image]\n    \"`vm` with `image` attached by the kernel's `attach-image` under its\n     own contract; an image already held is not attached twice.\")\n\n  (lift-closure\n    [vm closure encode]\n    \"The `:yin.k/closure` marker of `closure` in `vm`'s coordinates,\n     captured values encoded by `encode`, with `:yin.k/store-of` when the\n     closure carries one. Throws the `:yin.k/non-portable` refusal as\n     ex-data when the closure cannot be lifted.\")\n\n  (lower-closure\n    [vm marker decode]\n    \"The closure `marker` denotes in `vm`'s coordinates, captured values\n     decoded by `decode`, carrying the marker's `:yin.k/store-of`. A\n     marker of another binding discipline or format is\n     `:binding-mismatch`.\")\n\n  (gc-roots\n    [vm]\n    \"This kernel's registers as heap-reclamation root values, each a whole\n     register, never selected keys, so no root is missed here:\n     `{:kernel [...] :values [...]}`. A `:kernel` register holds this\n     kernel's own shapes (a continuation, the control); a `:values`\n### 3.3 Where and when the validator runs\n\n**DECIDED** (carrier order kept: draft §8, step 7 after step 6; the\nreview's ruling). On **lower**: gate (1), structure (2), graph (3),\nhashes (4), canonical form (5), canonical numbering (6), **frames (7)**,\npending and operations (8), dependency closure (9), custody (10),\ncomposition (11), restore (12). In step 7 the body's decoded task\ncontext is judged first by `frame/task-defect` (X1), then every `:act`,\n`:tail`, `:kframe`, `:reified` and parked-table state is decoded and\njudged by `frame/defect` with its context and that task context; a defect\nis `:yin.k/undecodable` with the rule's kind and the row path. A\nfirst-defect test therefore sees a numbering defect\n(`:noncanonical-cursor-cells`) before a frame defect on a body that has both,\nand §8's acceptance items say so. On **lift**: the same function runs\nover every assembled frame before any row is emitted; a frame the\nevaluator itself minted that fails is `:yin.k/non-portable`\n`:inconsistent-state`. The harness runs it over every frame a layout\nreconstructs.\n- **de Bruijn kernels**: the kernel's own `:free-env` field, \"fixed for\n  this instance\" (`stack.cljc:82`; `register.cljc:50`), read directly.\n- **the semantic-register kernel**: the evaluator keeps only the\n  mutable-current `:env` (`RegisterVM` field `env`, \"persistent lexical\n  scope map\", `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:23`; the old semantic\n  VM likewise captures the initial env only transiently in `eval`,\n  `semantic.cljc:874-876`), so no field holds the initial map. The\n  **composition owns it**: it is the value the composition passed as\n  `create-vm`'s `:env` (`vm/check-bindings!` of it, `:261`). The lift's\n  input contract therefore takes it explicitly,\n  `(rows/lift-task vm serve! {:free-env E₀})`, and refuses\n  `:yin.k/non-portable :missing-free-env` when the caller supplies none;\n  the holder and REPL paths that call the lift pass the environment they\n  constructed the task with. **Coordinated retention seam, recommended**:\n  4b (stage 3, its track's file) adds an immutable `free-env` field set\n  once in `create-vm` from the checked `:env` and never written by any\n  transition, with `gc-roots` listing it; once it lands the lift reads\n  it when `:free-env` is not supplied and the explicit argument stays as\n  the override for compositions that constructed the task elsewhere.\n  Phase 6 does **not** edit `semantic_register.cljc`; 6b depends on the\n  explicit argument and names the seam as a follow-up (§8.2).\n\nMerkle sharing means every `E` whose bindings equal another's shares one\n`:bindings` row; the root slot is one more reference to a row that\nusually already exists.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Lift and lower\n\n### 7.1 Lift\n\n**DECIDED** (draft §9, UCF §7.8): refuse unless quiescent; refuse the\nholds (`unliftable-hold`, `handoff.cljc:588`) as `:yin.k/non-portable\n:reason-mismatch`; classify kind; run the **dependency closure over the\n`\"v4\"` vectors**, which needs the phase-5 scanners\n(`scan/requirements`, `scan/free-names`, `scan/free-occurrences` over the\n§2.3 table: the current `completion/code-facts` reads stack-table\npositions and cannot be used), and refuse `:yin.k/unsatisfied` unless\n`:complete`, `:yin.k/trees` included; number cursor cells (draft §6); walk\nwaits, parked records, the store slice, module stores, the free\nenvironment (from the kernel's `:free-env` field or the lift's explicit\n`:free-env` argument, §6.3, never from a current `E`), the result,\ninstall children; run `frame/defect` over every\nframe; emit rows and the census. A de Bruijn source walks the frames\n`layout/lift-act`/`lift-tail` reconstruct.\n\n### 7.2 Lower\n\n**DECIDED** (draft §8 in order; §3.3): gate, structure, graph, hashes,\ncanonical form, canonical numbering, **frames**, pending and operations,\ndependency closure (`requires`/`code` agree with the census;\n`:yin.k/trees` complete per §6.1), custody, composition, restore. Restore\nbuilds the receiving kernel's state: semantic-register: `code` through\n`load-vector`/`attach-image` under `code/contract`, the free environment\nas base `:env`, each `:wait` to an engine entry (payload plus the\npending's engine fields, `lower-frame!`'s shapes, `handoff.cljc:3182-3246`,\n`:deliver` carried), parked records into `:parked`, the result into\n`:value`; de Bruijn: derive and attach the image for each A, set\n`:free-env`, and `layout/lower-act`/`lower-tail` each frame (the stack\nlane's `tail` needs 6c-pre). Restoration delivers nothing, runs nothing,\nmints nothing.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Slices, gates, entry conditions\n\nVerification follows `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`: G0 per iteration on\nthe JVM, G1 `bb test:sub yin.vm` on three hosts, G2 `bb test:changed`,\nG3 on master.\n\n### 8.1 Slice 6a: the frame validator and the row codec (independent)\n\n**Files to create.**\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc` (§3): `defect`, public.\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` (§2): the row table as data,\n  `frame->rows`, `rows->frame`, row ids (Jing default), the census and\n  numbering per the draft §6, `canonical-under` (§5.5, test-only but\n  placed here so three test namespaces share it). **Not** `lift-task`/\n  `lower-task`: full task transport is 6b.\n- `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame_test.cljc`,\n  `test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc`.\n\n**Depends on:** phase 3, 4a (landed), 4b stage 1 (branch) for live\nframes to validate. Touches nothing of 4b or 5; needs no scanner.\n\n**Acceptance (6a).**\n\n1. `frame-test/contract-is-pure`: `frame/defect` takes `[frame code\n   context task]`, `task` being plain data; the namespace's `ns` form\n   requires no kernel and no `yin.vm.engine` (a string check over the\n(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.scan\n  \"Dependency facts derived from admitted semantic register vectors.\"\n  (:require [dao.space.query :as query]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn :as debruijn]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]))\n\n\n(defn- bodies\n  [v]\n  (when-let [defect (code/well-formed? v)]\n    (throw (ex-info \"Cannot scan malformed semantic register vector\" defect)))\n  (code/parse v))\n\n\n(defn- chain\n  [v bs i]\n  (if-let [owner (:owner (nth bs i))]\n    (cons (nth (nth v owner) 2) (chain v bs (code/body-index bs owner)))\n    []))\n\n\n(defn free-occurrences\n  \"Free names with exact pc and closure enclosure, in emission order.\"\n  [v]\n  (let [bs (bodies v)]\n    (vec (keep-indexed\n           (fn [pc t]\n             (when (= :var (first t))\n               (let [name (nth t 2) i (code/body-index bs pc)]\n                 ;; Unreachable today: `bodies` runs `code/well-formed?`,\n                 ;; which refuses a `:var` naming a reserved name, and\n                 ;; lowering emits `:define`, never `:var yin/def`. Kept\n                 ;; so Rule R does not rest on the validator alone.\n                 (when (and (not (vm/reserved-name? name))\n                            (contains? (debruijn/resolve-name (chain v bs i) name) :free))\n                   {:name name :at pc :in-body? (pos? i)})))) v))))\n\n\n(defn free-names\n  \"The set of free names.\"\n  [v]\n  (set (map :name (free-occurrences v))))\n\n\n(defn definition-occurrences\n  \"Store writes with pc and conditional enclosure.\"\n  [v]\n  (let [bs (bodies v)\n        ranges (into #{} (mapcat (fn [[pc target]]\n                                   (range (inc (min pc target)) (max pc target))))\n                     (keep-indexed (fn [pc t]\n                                     (case (first t)\n                                       :jump [pc (nth t 1)]\n                                       :branch-false [pc (nth t 2)]\n                                       nil)) v))]\n    (vec (keep-indexed\n           (fn [pc t]\n             (when (contains? #{:store-put :define} (first t))\n               {:name (nth t 2) :at pc\n                :conditional? (or (contains? ranges pc)\n                                  (pos? (code/body-index bs pc)))})) v))))\n\n\n(defn application-sites\n  \"Call and FFI sites in pc order.\"\n  [v]\n  (bodies v)\n  (vec (keep-indexed (fn [pc t]\n                       (when (contains? #{:call :ffi-call} (first t)) {:at pc})) v)))\n\n\n(def footprint-mnemonics\n  \"Effect normalization under the current register vector table.\"\n  (dissoc (get-in vm/footprint-table [vm/semantic-contract :mnemonics]) :push))\n\n\n(defn segment-rows\n  \"Segment-qualified tuples addressed by A.\"\n  [v]\n  (bodies v)\n  (let [a (ucf/code-address v)]\n    (mapv (fn [pc t] (into [a pc] t)) (range) v)))\n\n\n(defn requirements\n  \"Datalog extraction of store, FFI, parked and effect requirements.\"\n  [v]\n  (let [db (query/relation (segment-rows v))\n        extract (fn [q] (set (map first (query/collect (query/q q db)))))\n        mnemonics (extract '[:find ?mn :in $code :where [$code _ _ ?mn & _]])]\n    {:store-keys (extract '[:find ?key :in $code\n                            :where (or [$code _ _ :store-get _ ?key]\n                                       [$code _ _ :store-put _ ?key _]\n                                       [$code _ _ :define _ ?key _])])\n     :ffi-ops (extract '[:find ?op :in $code :where [$code _ _ :ffi-call _ ?op _]])\n     :parked-ids (extract '[:find ?pid :in $code :where [$code _ _ :resume ?pid _]])\n     :effects (into #{} (mapcat footprint-mnemonics) mnemonics)}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
